course: dictionary
lesson: 12928
title: Evangelical: church words and keen words
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a special area of life, like church. «Evangelical» is one of them, and its meaning can change with the subject. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
explain: In church talk, «The evangelical church had lively singing and Bible study every Sunday.» The clues are singing and Bible study, which show what kind of church it is: one that puts great weight on the Bible and on personal faith.
explain: Outside church, the word means very keen and eager. «Mia is evangelical about recycling; she has told the whole class three times this week.» Telling the whole class three times is the clue: she is eager to win everyone over to her cause.
fact: Evangelical is an adjective (it describes a thing) and a noun (it names a person).
fact: In church talk, «evangelical» describes Christians who put great weight on the Bible, on personal faith in Jesus, and on telling others the good news.
fact: «An evangelical» is a person who belongs to this kind of Christianity.
fact: Outside church, «evangelical» means very keen and eager to persuade others about something you believe in, like a cause or a hobby.
fact: Useful phrases: evangelical church, evangelical Christian, evangelical zeal.
exercise: «The evangelical church held a Bible study every Thursday.» What does evangelical describe here? | A shop that sells old books | A church with a very tall tower | A school that closes early | *A church that puts great weight on the Bible and personal faith
exercise: «Sam is evangelical about football; he talks about it at every break.» What does evangelical mean here? | Bored of all sport | *Very keen and eager to tell others about it | Afraid of playing football | Good at playing in goal
exercise: In church talk, what is «an evangelical»? | *A person who belongs to this kind of Christianity | A kind of bird that sings at dawn | A teacher who runs a school choir | A type of old song
test: «Her evangelical zeal made everyone want to try recycling.» What does zeal show about her? | Anger at a broken window | *Great enthusiasm | Fear of the weather | Sleepiness
test: Which phrase names a church that stresses Bible study and sharing faith? | paper round | village hall | glass house | *evangelical church
exam: Which meaning fits in «The evangelical speaker begged everyone to join the cause»? | A speaker from another country | A speaker who is very quiet and shy | A speaker who sings in a choir | *Keen and eager to persuade others
